; 01-apply-an-implication-modus-ponens.kurt
;
; Apply an implication: modus ponens
;
; If the theory contains `A implies B` and `A`, write `B`. Kurt applies implication elimination
; automatically.

bool A, B, C

use A implies B  "A-to-B"
use A
B

use B implies C  "B-to-C"
C

; Kurt performs one inference step at a time. It derives `B` first and can then use that new fact
; to derive `C`.
